WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.897
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:08.770
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:13.556
Unit six: My Neighborhood. Today you will describe places in your neighborhood.

4
00:00:13.856 --> 00:00:16.532
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.769
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:22.664
Neighborhood.

7
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.963
Neighborhood means the area around your home.

8
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.143
My neighborhood is quiet.

9
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.379
Your turn. Say: Neighborhood.

10
00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.478
Neighborhood.

11
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:37.206
Resident.

12
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:40.832
Resident means a person who lives in a place.

13
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.706
The residents keep the street clean.

14
00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:46.528
Your turn. Say: Resident.

15
00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:50.437
Resident.

16
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:52.219
Landmark.

17
00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:56.261
Landmark means a famous place that is easy to see.

18
00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.850
The pagoda is a local landmark.

19
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.615
Your turn. Say: Landmark.

20
00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:05.561
Landmark.

21
00:01:06.317 --> 00:01:07.689
Convenience store.

22
00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:11.797
Convenience store means a small shop that is open late.

23
00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:14.592
I buy water at the convenience store.

24
00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:18.230
Your turn. Say: Convenience store.

25
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.869
Convenience store.

26
00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:24.432
Crowded.

27
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:27.254
Crowded means full of people.

28
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.791
The market is crowded in the morning.

29
00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:32.873
Your turn. Say: Crowded.

30
00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:36.572
Crowded.

31
00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:38.295
Peaceful.

32
00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:41.144
Peaceful means quiet and calm.

33
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.842
The riverside is peaceful at night.

34
00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.859
Your turn. Say: Peaceful.

35
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.597
Peaceful.

36
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.328
Nearby.

37
00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:55.119
Nearby means not far away.

38
00:01:55.717 --> 00:01:57.252
There's a school nearby.

39
00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.212
Your turn. Say: Nearby.

40
00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.370
Nearby.

41
00:02:05.117 --> 00:02:06.454
Public transport.

42
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:11.040
Public transport means buses and trains that everyone can use.

43
00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.218
Phnom Penh has city buses for public transport.

44
00:02:14.817 --> 00:02:17.655
Your turn. Say: Public transport.

45
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.733
Public transport.

46
00:02:22.483 --> 00:02:23.635
Intersection.

47
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.729
Intersection means a place where two roads cross.

48
00:02:28.317 --> 00:02:30.119
Turn left at the intersection.

49
00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.253
Your turn. Say: Intersection.

50
00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.415
Intersection.

51
00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.592
Community center.

52
00:02:40.583 --> 00:02:43.744
Community center means a building where local people meet.

53
00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.976
There are dance classes at the community center.

54
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:50.944
Your turn. Say: Community center.

55
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.265
Community center.

56
00:02:56.017 --> 00:02:56.844
Safe.

57
00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.583
Safe means not dangerous.

58
00:03:00.183 --> 00:03:01.986
Our street is safe for children.

59
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:04.980
Your turn. Say: Safe.

60
00:03:07.833 --> 00:03:08.846
Safe.

61
00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:10.433
Modern.

62
00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.390
Modern means new and using the latest ideas.

63
00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:16.739
There's a modern shopping mall.

64
00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.759
Your turn. Say: Modern.

65
00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.485
Modern.

66
00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.473
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:29.317 --> 00:03:31.351
Visal, what's your neighborhood like?

68
00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:35.973
It's peaceful. There is a beautiful pagoda nearby.

69
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.456
Are there any shops?

70
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.790
Yes, there are two convenience stores and a crowded market.

71
00:03:44.883 --> 00:03:45.919
Is it safe?

72
00:03:47.017 --> 00:03:50.946
Yes, it's very safe. There is a friendly community center too.

73
00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.995
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:58.637
Grammar focus: There is and There are plus adjectives.

75
00:03:58.937 --> 00:04:00.310
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:01.017 --> 00:04:02.610
There is a peaceful park.

77
00:04:03.517 --> 00:04:05.319
There are many friendly residents.

78
00:04:06.217 --> 00:04:07.984
There is a modern mall nearby.

79
00:04:08.933 --> 00:04:13.301
Put the adjective before the noun: a peaceful park — not a park peaceful.

80
00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:17.457
Be careful! Don't say: There is a park peaceful.

81
00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.643
Say: There is a peaceful park.

82
00:04:21.943 --> 00:04:23.734
Put the adjective before the noun.

83
00:04:24.533 --> 00:04:27.128
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:29.062
Where I Live.

85
00:04:29.362 --> 00:04:31.513
My neighborhood is peaceful and safe.

86
00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:37.402
There is a convenience store nearby, and there is a crowded market at the intersection.

87
00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.537
There is a community center where residents often gather.

88
00:04:42.533 --> 00:04:45.253
There are buses for public transport on the main road.

89
00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:49.056
I like living here because the people are friendly.

90
00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:54.250
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:56.897
There blank many residents.

92
00:04:57.197 --> 00:05:00.421
A, are. B, is. C, be.

93
00:05:03.967 --> 00:05:05.943
The answer is A: are.

94
00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:09.617
A place where two roads cross is an blank.

95
00:05:09.917 --> 00:05:13.977
A, intersection. B, landmark. C, resident.

96
00:05:17.533 --> 00:05:19.753
The answer is A: intersection.

97
00:05:20.917 --> 00:05:22.405
Full of people is blank.

98
00:05:22.705 --> 00:05:25.848
A, crowded. B, peaceful. C, safe.

99
00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.167
The answer is A: crowded.

100
00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:35.600
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.484
What do you like most about your neighborhood?

102
00:05:47.283 --> 00:05:48.795
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:49.095 --> 00:05:55.997
I like the peaceful park most. There is a modern library nearby too, and the residents are very friendly.

104
00:05:56.297 --> 00:05:57.995
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:05:58.883 --> 00:06:04.032
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and there is and there are plus adjectives.

106
00:06:04.332 --> 00:06:08.900
Today's value is community spirit. Help and care for people in your town.

107
00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.620
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

108
00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:15.141
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

